//ERR 16 3 16 6
//MSG="This function does not return a value in all control paths"

// The loop exemption has a limit. A `while true` is the one loop the check may
// treat as never falling through — see 29_while_true_returns_from_inside.cpl —
// but that only holds while nothing can leave it. The `brk` here is a second
// exit, so the end of the body is reachable after all and `f(1000)` would run
// off it.
//
// The exemption is therefore not "the condition is the literal `true`" but "the
// condition is the literal `true` and no `brk` targets this loop".
// 31_a_while_true_with_a_break_returns_after_the_loop.cpl is the accepted form —
// the same function with a `ret -1` at the end — and
// 32_a_break_from_an_inner_loop_does_not_escape_a_while_true.cpl is the `brk`
// that belongs to some other loop and so does not count.

fn f n
    i = 0
    while true
        if i > 10
            brk
        if i * i > n
            ret i
        i++

fn main
    out "{f(1000)}"
